      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Seedream 5 → HDR\n\n1. ByteDance Seedream 4.5 & 5.0 generates the image through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt.\n3. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n4. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n5. Write EXR saves a 32-bit float EXR: the master as beauty and rudra.reconstructed as its own channel. Output: output/radiance_api/."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Seedream 5 → HDR\n\n1. ByteDance Seedream 4.5 & 5.0 generates the image through ComfyUI's API nodes (sign in to your Comfy account; the run uses API credits). Edit the prompt and settings there.\n2. SDR → HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2 (Auto, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run): a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the generated codes. reconstructed_mask marks where light was rebuilt.\n3. SDR → HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) is bypassed. Select it and press Ctrl+B to regenerate large blown highlights (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU; downloaded on first use).\n4. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 against the SDR source: use the wipe to see what RUDRA rebuilt.\n5. Write EXR saves a 32-bit float EXR: the master as beauty and rudra.reconstructed as its own channel. Output: output/radiance_api/."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
